id=\"internal-link\"><div data-testid=\"edinburgh-video\"><div data-testid=\"card-media-wrapper\"><div data-testid=\"card-media\"><p><img src=\"https://static.files.bbci.co.uk/bbcdotcom/web/20260407-092955-f3cfe0ee04-web-3.0.0-2/grey-placeholder.png\" aria-label=\"image unavailable\"><img sizes=\"(min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1008px) 25vw, (min-width: 800px) 33vw, 50vw\" srcset=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp 1536w\" src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/6a97/live/c51718a0-30e3-11f0-8519-3b5a01ebe413.jpg.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"A screenshot of a CCTV video showing Palestinians running away following an Israeli airstrike which hit the European hospital in Gaza. A crater can be seen in the background. BBC Verify's logo is in the top left-hand corner.\"></p></div></div><div data-testid=\"card-text-wrapper\"><div><p><h2 data-testid=\"card-headline\">Israeli 'bunker buster' bombs used in Gaza hospital strike, experts say</h2></p></div><p data-testid=\"card-description\">CCTV footage obtained and verified by the BBC shows the moment before impact and the immediate aftermath. Munitions experts told BBC Verify that the strikes and destruction are consistent with the use of so-called \"bunker buster\" bombs - designed to hit underground targets. BBC Verify's Merlyn Thomas has more.</p><p><span data-testid=\"card-metadata-tag\">BBC Verify</span></p></div></div></a></div><div data-testid=\"edinburgh-card\" data-indexcard=\"true\"><a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/videos/c9dj44v4eqwo\" data-testid=\"internal-link\"><div data-testid=\"edinburgh-video\"><div data-testid=\"card-media-wrapper\"><div data-testid=\"card-media\"><p><img src=\"https://static.files.bbci.co.uk/bbcdotcom/web/20260407-092955-f3cfe0ee04-web-3.0.0-2/grey-placeholder.png\" aria-label=\"image unavailable\"><img sizes=\"(min-width: 1280px) 20vw, (min-width: 1008px) 25vw, (min-width: 800px) 33vw, 50vw\" srcset=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp 1536w\" src=\"https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/dee0/live/283db810-21eb-11f0-8c2e-77498b1ce297.png.webp\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"BBC Verify reporter Merlyn Thomas standing in front of a map of Ukraine and Russa, with areas under Russian control highlighted in red\"></p></div></div><div data-testid=\"card-text-wrapper\"><div><p><h2 data-testid=\"card-headline\">What would it mean for Ukraine to temporarily give up land?</h2></p></div><p data-testid=\"card-description\">As Ukraine reckons with the terms of a possible peace deal, BBC Verify asks what it could mean in practice.</p><p><span data-testid=\"card-metadata-tag\">B